plugin-hostd (0.15.8) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Release 0.15.8: with #365, a chain that does not form says why
  * ci: the Zynthian chain job installs from the channel the other jobs use
  * docs/protocol: chain_stalled, as tools/protocol-doc.py writes it
  * profile: row 6, a worker's PSS is the JACK shm segment, not its libraries
  * supervisor: chain_stalled names what holds a chain that does not form
    within chain_form_timeout_ms
  * daemon test: a chain that does not form is said once with the member, the
    step and the code that held it (red)
  * docs/zynthian: the LV2 pin counts broken down
  * docs/zynthian: add-time and cold-start figures like for like,
    qualification counts that add up
  * bench: the 24 plugins on the LV2 builds everywhere; evidence:
    like-for-like rows and the cold-to-snapshot document
  * bench: a chain add the chain refuses is added own, as Zynthian does; the
    ten third-party set; the Pi add rows of 2026-11-01
  * docs: Zynthian pages take the add rows, cold-snapshot rows and final
    qualification counts
  * Release 0.15.8
  * lv2, qualcost: a repeat lookup reads one manifest and lists no directory
    again
  * packaging: the omx-clap-core contract floor stays where it was;
    chain_expect is used only by a worker that answers it
  * fuzz: the add property knows the chain placement; a sabotage anchor that
    the chain_expect drop path repeats is made unique
  * docs: a profile note, the ranked list of measured costs and the next cut
  * omx-clap-core 0.26.0's verbs render: chain_expect, and the contract floor
    it needs
  * supervisor: a chain member after the first is expected into the chain's
    walk (chain_expect), no client of its own (#348)
  * fuzz records and a sabotage anchor follow the chain placement in verbs.c
    and add (#348)
  * bench: chain-add mode and a 24-plugin cvp scenario: add time with no
    worker per plugin (#348)
  * supervisor: add <uri> <inst> chain:<n> puts the plugin into the chain's
    worker (#348)
  * docs: the channel strip example gives both ways: separate plugins and omx
    strip
  * docs: Zynthian pages take the engine's proof on the Pi, omx-clap-host
    0.25.4 and the Mixbus medians
  * docs: status: the Pi's Zynthian as it runs today, and the proofs the
    grouping fixes passed there
  * docs: status names what the Pi runs now and what is released beyond it
  * docs: ten third-party plugins in a group belong in what you get
  * mixbus-bench: a chain that does not form is linked member by member, and
    a stereo third-party set
  * mixbus-bench: the crash row wires through the daemon, which replays its
    own connections
  * mixbus-bench: the crash row strikes its notes again and watches the
    killed client
  * voices-cores: absolute paths for the daemon's workers, and the card
    without device reservation
  * voices-cores: a private server on a real card
  * tools/zynthian: a shared effect against an effect per chain, a parallel
    pair, and a worker killed under notes
  * bench: chains vs processes with the LV2 builds on every host, like for
    like
  * bench: chains vs processes with CLAP plugins only, which a chain shares
    one JACK client for
  * pools-bench: the sine client's port names, and it no longer feeds
    playback directly
  * tools/zynthian: the same plugins as a worker each, a few pools, one pool
  * voices-cores: read the level from before the notes, for drums
  * voices-cores: notes through a program's own shell, and the voices it
    counts
  * bench: the JACK server's context switches, and chains vs processes up to
    48 plugins

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Sun, 01 Nov 2026 20:27:22 +0000
